{"segs": ["PA_ja_103:0.2", "PA_ja_103:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Parosatavagga (The Chapter on More than One Hundred)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_103:0.4"], "en": "3. The Veri-jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_103:1.1", "PA_ja_103:1.2"], "en": "“Where an enemy dwells, there a wise person should not live.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_103:1.3"], "en": "\"For one night or two nights,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_103:1.4"], "en": "an enemy dwells in misery.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_103:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the third Jātaka, the Verijātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
